      "dedupe_key": "story-of-music-hall|2026-10-06|headstone-manor",
      "description": "Take a lively trip through the rise of the British Music Hall, meeting the colourful stars whose songs and cheeky humour charmed a nation. With stories, scandals, sparkle and a chance to sing along to some familiar favourites - it’s an irresistible journey into a world that still delights today. About the Speaker: Judy Karbritz is Harrow's Community Poet and writes regular columns for the Harrow Times and Barnet Borough Times. She has broadcast on LBC and local BBC radio and performed in amateur dramatics. She has been giving entertaining talks for twenty years and performs locally and regularly speaks on cruise ships.",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://harrow-arts.transforms.svdcdn.com/production/HMM/Whats-On-Autumn-26/1780169711974blob.jpg?w=640&h=360&q=100&auto=format&fit=crop&dm=1784556300&s=0d8f5f8cd3bb6b40412b9c51fe90ca78",
