  {
    "event": {
      "address": "Headstone Recreation Ground, Pinner View, Harrow HA2 6PX",
      "all_day": false,
      "category": "community",
      "dedupe_key": "exploring-harrows-wartime-bomb-map|2026-11-10|headstone-manor",
      "description": "Harrow's wartime bomb map is one of the most remarkable local records to survive the Second World War; colour-coded street by street to document exactly what the Blitz, the Doodlebugs and the V2 rockets did to the borough and its people. We are delighted to offer guided talks at our brand-new interactive bomb-damage map, a remarkable survival from the Second World War that recorded, street by street and house by house, exactly what the bombing of Harrow looked like. Colour-coded under official wartime instruction, the map tells the story not just of destruction but of the families displaced, and the extraordinary effort by ordinary people to keep the borough functioning through some of the darkest years in living memory. Our knowledgeable guide will lead you through the map's hidden language: what each colour meant, which weapons caused which damage, and how the record was used for everything from rehousing applications to hospital planning. Whether you have family roots in the area or are simply curious about the history beneath today's streets, this is a rare chance to see Harrow's wartime experience close up, in vivid and human detail.",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://harrow-arts.transforms.svdcdn.com/production/HMM/Whats-On-Autumn-26/IMG_20260602_141758.jpg?w=640&h=360&q=100&auto=format&fit=crop&dm=1784554523&s=0211940955acf32e1256f214d3976e6b",
      "lat": 51.5947,
      "lng": -0.3542,
      "price": {
        "currency": "GBP",
        "is_free": false,
        "max": "3",
        "min": "3"
      },
      "starts_at": "2026-11-10T10:00:00Z",
      "tags": [],
      "title": "Exploring Harrow’s Wartime Bomb Map",
      "url": "https://headstonemanor.org/events/hmm-exploring-harrows-wartime-bomb-map",
      "venue_name": "Headstone Manor & Museum"
    },
    "id": "events/hmm-exploring-harrows-wartime-bomb-map",
    "payload": {
      "description": "<p>Harrow's wartime bomb map is one of the most remarkable local records to survive the Second World War; colour-coded street by street to document exactly what the Blitz, the Doodlebugs and the V2 rockets did to the borough and its people.</p><p>We are delighted to offer guided talks at our brand-new interactive bomb-damage map, a remarkable survival from the Second World War that recorded, street by street and house by house, exactly what the bombing of Harrow looked like. Colour-coded under official wartime instruction, the map tells the story not just of destruction but of the families displaced, and the extraordinary effort by ordinary people to keep the borough functioning through some of the darkest years in living memory.</p><p>Our knowledgeable guide will lead you through the map's hidden language: what each colour meant, which weapons caused which damage, and how the record was used for everything from rehousing applications to hospital planning. Whether you have family roots in the area or are simply curious about the history beneath today's streets, this is a rare chance to see Harrow's wartime experience close up, in vivid and human detail.</p>",
      "duration": "45 minutes",
      "end": null,
      "genre": "Events for Adults",
      "image_url": "https://harrow-arts.transforms.svdcdn.com/production/HMM/Whats-On-Autumn-26/IMG_20260602_141758.jpg?w=640&h=360&q=100&auto=format&fit=crop&dm=1784554523&s=0211940955acf32e1256f214d3976e6b",
      "path": "/events/hmm-exploring-harrows-wartime-bomb-map",
      "pre_title": null,
      "price_text": "£3 per person",
      "room": "Meeting point: entrance to The Manor House",
      "start": "2026-11-10T10:00:00+00:00",
      "title": "Exploring Harrow’s Wartime Bomb Map",
      "url": "https://headstonemanor.org/events/hmm-exploring-harrows-wartime-bomb-map"
    }
  },
  {
    "event": {
      "address": "Headstone Recreation Ground, Pinner View, Harrow HA2 6PX",
      "all_day": false,
      "category": "talk",
      "dedupe_key": "impact-of-americans-coming-to-england-eastcote-during-ww2|2026-11-10|headstone-manor",
      "description": "Codebreaking played a crucial role in the Allied victory during the Second World War. Yet few people realise just how closely American and British personnel worked together to decipher Nazi Germany's encoded messages. This presentation explores the vital contribution of the Americans who came to England, and specifically to Eastcote, during the war. Discover how they were recruited and trained, and how they worked alongside British servicemen and women in one of the most secret and important intelligence operations of the conflict. The talk also examines the friendly rivalry between Britain and the United States, and how this competitive spirit was channelled into a highly effective partnership. Attendees will have the opportunity to view a collection of rare photographs of American personnel working at Eastcote, uncovered through the speaker's extensive research and previously unseen by GCHQ Museum archivists. Learn about the achievements of the Wrens and their American naval counterparts across the Atlantic, whose dedication, skill and determination helped shorten the war and contribute to the Allied victory. About the Speaker: Ronald Koorm has published four books on Military history, codebreaking, and has given numerous talks to museums, history societies, Universities, libraries, and other organisations.",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://harrow-arts.transforms.svdcdn.com/production/HMM/Whats-On-Autumn-26/bombe-wave-bw-ncm-2016-107w-1.jpg?w=640&h=360&q=100&auto=format&fit=crop&dm=1784557060&s=e00757dd557059c6e02edbaf839a5228",
      "lat": 51.5947,
      "lng": -0.3542,
      "price": {
        "currency": "GBP",
        "is_free": false,
        "max": "4.50",
        "min": "4.50"
      },
      "starts_at": "2026-11-10T14:00:00Z",
      "tags": [],
      "title": "The Impact of the Americans coming to England and Eastcote during WW2",
      "url": "https://headstonemanor.org/events/hmm-tuesday-talk-the-impact-of-the-americans-coming-to-england-and-eastcote-during-ww2",
      "venue_name": "Headstone Manor & Museum"
    },
    "id": "events/hmm-tuesday-talk-the-impact-of-the-americans-coming-to-england-and-eastcote-during-ww2",
    "payload": {
      "description": "<p>Codebreaking played a crucial role in the Allied victory during the Second World War. Yet few people realise just how closely American and British personnel worked together to decipher Nazi Germany's encoded messages.</p><p>This presentation explores the vital contribution of the Americans who came to England, and specifically to Eastcote, during the war. Discover how they were recruited and trained, and how they worked alongside British servicemen and women in one of the most secret and important intelligence operations of the conflict.</p><p>The talk also examines the friendly rivalry between Britain and the United States, and how this competitive spirit was channelled into a highly effective partnership. Attendees will have the opportunity to view a collection of rare photographs of American personnel working at Eastcote, uncovered through the speaker's extensive research and previously unseen by GCHQ Museum archivists.</p><p>Learn about the achievements of the Wrens and their American naval counterparts across the Atlantic, whose dedication, skill and determination helped shorten the war and contribute to the Allied victory.</p><p><strong>About the Speaker:</strong></p><p>Ronald Koorm has published four books on Military history, codebreaking, and has given numerous talks to museums, history societies, Universities, libraries, and other organisations.</p>",
      "duration": "60 minutes",
      "end": null,
      "genre": "Events for Adults",
      "image_url": "https://harrow-arts.transforms.svdcdn.com/production/HMM/Whats-On-Autumn-26/bombe-wave-bw-ncm-2016-107w-1.jpg?w=640&h=360&q=100&auto=format&fit=crop&dm=1784557060&s=e00757dd557059c6e02edbaf839a5228",
      "path": "/events/hmm-tuesday-talk-the-impact-of-the-americans-coming-to-england-and-eastcote-during-ww2",
      "pre_title": "Tuesday Talk",
      "price_text": "£4.50 per person",
      "room": "The Granary",
      "start": "2026-11-10T14:00:00+00:00",
      "title": "The Impact of the Americans coming to England and Eastcote during WW2",
      "url": "https://headstonemanor.org/events/hmm-tuesday-talk-the-impact-of-the-americans-coming-to-england-and-eastcote-during-ww2"
    }
