      "dedupe_key": "stained-glass-suncatcher-workshop|2026-11-29|headstone-manor",
      "description": "Create a stained glass suncatcher with artist Suzanne Raffellini using the copperfoil (Tiffany) technique—the perfect handmade gift for Christmas or treasured decoration for your home. What to Expect Create a beautiful stained glass suncatcher using the copperfoil (Tiffany) technique – the perfect handmade gift for Christmas or a treasured decoration for your home. During this relaxing, therapeutic workshop, you'll learn to cut and shape glass, wrap pieces with copperfoil, and solder them together to create a stunning suncatcher. Choose from pre-designed patterns or create your own. All skills taught from scratch with small group demonstrations and individual support – no experience needed. Beginners and experienced makers welcome. Work at your own pace and take your finished piece home the same day. Suzanne Raffellini is a full-time glass artist who sells her work through her website www.suzanneraffelliniglassartist.com and at craft fairs such as Waddesdon Christmas Market and Handmade in Chelsea. She takes on commission work such as the front entrance of St. Michael’s and All Angels Church in Amersham and other private residences. She also teaches regular weekly classes at Bellingdon Village Hall, one day workshops, covering a variety of topics, and fully immersive summer schools at her Chesham Studio. This course is supported by our Council Partner, Learn Harrow. To take part, you’ll need to book with them directly here. You can read their privacy policy here.",
